  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0325_f785ba69e89c.png\" style=\"width: 296px; height: 184px;\" /><br /><br />Assuming potential at B = 0, then w.r.t. B the potential of other points are as shown in figure then<br /><br />So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>"
